&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Anduril Industries is a defense technology company with a mission to transform U.S. and allied military capabilities with advanced technology. By bringing the expertise, technology, and business model of the 21st century’s most innovative companies to the defense industry, Anduril is changing how military systems are designed, built and sold. Anduril’s family of systems is powered by Lattice OS, an AI-powered operating system that turns thousands of data streams into a realtime, 3D command and control center. As the world enters an era of strategic competition, Anduril is committed to bringing cutting-edge autonomy, AI, computer vision, sensor fusion, and networking technology to the military in months, not years.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Delivering that mission for our allies means being where they are. Corporate Technology International builds and runs the IT, infrastructure and security behind Anduril&#39;s growth in every market outside the United States. APAC is our largest region, with sites in Australia, Japan, South Korea and Taiwan&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Based in Sydney, you&#39;ll run Corporate Technology in APAC and own the region&#39;s results, people and budget as a peer to the Senior Manager, EMEA.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Run APAC Corporate Technology&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the region&#39;s IT service, infrastructure, security engineering and reliability teams: more than a dozen people, through three direct reports.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hire, performance manage and develop your managers, tech leads and engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work through the big architecture and design calls with your tech leads, across networks, identity, cloud, end-user computing and secure facilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan, advocate for and deliver the region&#39;s 12 to 24 month roadmap, budget and headcount plan as part of the Corporate Technology International plan, and approve hires and spend within it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be the first point of contact in APAC for business lines, divisions and site leadership, for escalations, priorities and new requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run a regular health review of the services your team runs in APAC. Take issues on systems other teams own to that team with the business impact, and track them until they&#39;re closed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hold the region to the standards set by global IT, Enterprise Systems, Infrastructure Engineering and Information Security, and work closely with Security and Trade Compliance. Where a country&#39;s laws or Defence customers need something different, agree the local approach with the owning team and keep everything else on the global standard.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Corporate Technology to Australian Government customers and partners, and work with Security on Anduril Australia&#39;s Defence Industry Security Program obligations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support the expansions team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the expansions team build and improve its playbook, and use it on APAC office moves and expansions, so each one is quicker and cheaper than the last.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring the region&#39;s operating needs into each new APAC site&#39;s design before work starts, so your team can support it from go-live.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release APAC people to work under the expansions team&#39;s direction on a deployments, and cover their day-to-day work while they&#39;re away.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan each go-live handover with the expansions team and the HQ teams that run each system, so your team takes the site over with support in place on day one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Size what each APAC site and market needs to run, from local headcount to support from HQ, so leadership knows what a market costs before committing to it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led managers or tech leads across more than one discipline, including hiring, performance management and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive hands-on experience as an engineer in infrastructure, networks, cloud, security or enterprise IT. You can question a design and hold your own with tech leads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the plan for work across several teams, including work where you had to define the problem first, and were held to its milestones and results&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivered technology change across more than one site or country, with the teams that own the systems and the infrastructure they run on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Changed the plans or priorities of senior leaders you didn&#39;t report to, and kept their trust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Been accountable for a service people use every day, with service targets, an escalation path and a budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represented your organisation to government customers or regulators, and written the plans and updates they worked from&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in engineering, computer science, information systems or a related field, or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Australian citizen, eligible to obtain and maintain an Australian Government Security Clearance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in defence, national security or another highly regulated industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Led teams across several Asia-Pacific countries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Worked with Australian Government security frameworks, such as the Protective Security Policy Framework (PSPF), Information Security Manual (ISM) and Defence Industry Security Program (DISP)&lt;/li&gt;
